---
// AgenticLab.astro
---

<section id="agentic" class="agentic-section">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-badge-row">
      <span class="badge badge-ai">🤖 Autonomous Agent Engineering</span>
      <span class="badge">Antigravity &amp; Claude Code Harnesses</span>
    </div>

    <div class="agentic-header">
      <h2 class="heading-lg agentic-title">
        The Agentic Lab: <span class="text-gradient-ai">Harnesses, MCP Servers &amp; Autonomous Loops</span>
      </h2>
      <p class="agentic-desc">
        AI coding assistants and autonomous multi-agent systems are not just prompt wrappers—they are distributed execution engines. In my daily engineering at NatWest and in open-source systems, I design and run agents using <strong>Google Antigravity</strong> and <strong>Claude Code</strong> harnesses, backed by production-grade <strong>Model Context Protocol (MCP)</strong> servers.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Agentic Architecture Diagram -->
    <div class="card arch-diagram-card">
      <div class="arch-diagram-title font-mono">PRODUCTION AGENTIC HARNESS TOPOLOGY</div>
      <div class="diagram-flow">
        <div class="diagram-step">
          <div class="step-badge badge-ai">1. Prompt &amp; Task</div>
          <div class="step-card">
            <div class="step-name">User / Event Trigger</div>
            <div class="step-sub">Complex business case, data anomaly, or batch job</div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="diagram-arrow">➔</div>

        <div class="diagram-step">
          <div class="step-badge badge-ai">2. Harness Loop</div>
          <div class="step-card highlight-harness">
            <div class="step-name">Antigravity / Claude Code</div>
            <div class="step-sub">Autonomous reasoning, sandbox isolation, reactive wakeups</div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="diagram-arrow">➔</div>

        <div class="diagram-step">
          <div class="step-badge badge-coffee">3. Protocol Layer</div>
          <div class="step-card">
            <div class="step-name">Custom MCP Servers</div>
            <div class="step-sub">Standardized JSON-RPC tools with Pydantic contracts</div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="diagram-arrow">➔</div>

        <div class="diagram-step">
          <div class="step-badge badge-data">4. Data Lakehouse</div>
          <div class="step-card">
            <div class="step-name">Snowflake / AWS / Postgres</div>
            <div class="step-sub">Jittered backoff, zero deployment lock contention</div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="diagram-arrow">➔</div>

        <div class="diagram-step">
          <div class="step-badge badge">5. Observability</div>
          <div class="step-card">
            <div class="step-name">Splunk &amp; LLM Judge</div>
            <div class="step-sub">Tool latency telemetry &amp; decision quality audits</div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Agentic Capabilities Grid -->
    <div class="agentic-grid">
      <div class="card capability-card">
        <div class="cap-header">
          <div class="cap-icon">⚙️</div>
          <h3 class="heading-sm cap-title">Custom Enterprise MCP Servers</h3>
        </div>
        <p class="cap-text">
          Designed and packaged reusable Model Context Protocol servers consumed across multiple downstream agents without repetitive data-access code. Exposing deterministic Python and SQL tools with strict Pydantic schemas.
        </p>
        <div class="cap-pill font-mono">JSON-RPC • Schema Contracts • Reusable Across Agents</div>
      </div>

      <div class="card capability-card">
        <div class="cap-header">
          <div class="cap-icon">🛡️</div>
          <h3 class="heading-sm cap-title">Antigravity &amp; Claude Code Workflows</h3>
        </div>
        <p class="cap-text">
          Building end-to-end autonomous loops. Using isolated workspaces, subagent delegation, deterministic validation tools, and reactive wakeups to ensure agents solve real engineering workflows reliably.
        </p>
        <div class="cap-pill font-mono">Subagent Tiering • Context Economy • Sandbox Isolation</div>
      </div>

      <div class="card capability-card">
        <div class="cap-header">
          <div class="cap-icon">📊</div>
          <h3 class="heading-sm cap-title">Enterprise Observability &amp; Safety</h3>
        </div>
        <p class="cap-text">
          Telemetry integrated into Splunk for agent execution trace, tool latency, and decision drift. Employing LLM-as-a-judge pipelines to continually evaluate grounding and compliance against UK banking standards.
        </p>
        <div class="cap-pill font-mono">Splunk Dashboards • LLM-as-a-Judge • 90% Manual Time Saved</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .agentic-section {
    padding: 5rem 0;
    position: relative;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
  }

  .agentic-header {
    margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
  }

  .agentic-title {
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .agentic-desc {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    max-width: 820px;
  }

  .agentic-desc strong {
    color: var(--text-primary);
  }

  .arch-diagram-card {
    background: linear-gradient(180deg, rgba(99, 102, 241, 0.05) 0%, var(--bg-card) 100%);
    border-color: rgba(99, 102, 241, 0.3);
    margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
    padding: 2rem;
  }

  .arch-diagram-title {
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    color: var(--accent-ai-light);
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
    text-align: center;
  }

  .diagram-flow {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 1rem;
    align-items: center;
  }

  @media (min-width: 960px) {
    .diagram-flow {
      flex-direction: row;
      justify-content: space-between;
      gap: 0.5rem;
    }
  }

  .diagram-step {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 190px;
  }

  .step-badge {
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
  }

  .step-card {
    width: 100%;
    background: var(--bg-tertiary);
    border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    padding: 0.85rem;
    text-align: center;
    transition: all 0.2s ease;
  }

  .highlight-harness {
    border-color: var(--accent-ai);
    background: rgba(99, 102, 241, 0.12);
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-glow-ai);
  }

  .step-name {
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    color: var(--text-primary);
    margin-bottom: 0.25rem;
  }

  .step-sub {
    font-size: 0.725rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    line-height: 1.35;
  }

  .diagram-arrow {
    color: var(--accent-ai-light);
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    transform: rotate(90deg);
  }

  @media (min-width: 960px) {
    .diagram-arrow {
      transform: rotate(0deg);
    }
  }

  .agentic-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    gap: 1.5rem;
  }

  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .agentic-grid {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    }
  }

  .capability-card {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.85rem;
  }

  .cap-header {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.75rem;
  }

  .cap-icon {
    font-size: 1.5rem;
  }

  .cap-title {
    color: var(--text-primary);
  }

  .cap-text {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    flex-grow: 1;
  }

  .cap-pill {
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    color: var(--accent-ai-light);
    background: var(--accent-ai-bg);
    padding: 0.35rem 0.65rem;
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
    border: 1px solid rgba(99, 102, 241, 0.2);
  }
</style>
